      "blurb": "Spider-like ambush predator with web-launching capability",
      "publicNotes": "<p>Lurkers are arachnoid predators that cling to walls and ceilings, waiting for prey to pass beneath them. They are fast, difficult to dislodge from vertical surfaces, and capable of firing biological webs that immobilize targets at range. In enclosed environments—cave systems, ship corridors, colony infrastructure—they are disproportionately dangerous. Open-field encounters are significantly easier to manage.</p><p><strong>Wall Crawler:</strong> The lurker can climb at full speed and is not flat-footed while doing so.</p><p><strong>Web Shot (2 actions):</strong> Ranged 30 ft. The target must succeed at a DC 18 Reflex save or become restrained (Escape DC 18). On a critical failure, the target is also immobilized until the web is destroyed (HP 5, AC 10).</p>",
